    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0930" n="892" xml:id="pg892"/>

                <head>368. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Canada<anchor n="1" xml:id="d368-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1957-05-28T20:14:00-04:00">May 28, 1957— 8:14
                        p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>442. Hope conclude Polish agreement<anchor n="2" xml:id="d368-f2"/> late this
                    week or early next week to provide: <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item>Eximbank component including about 100,000 MT wheat effective
                            immediately.</item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>Interim Title I no wheat effective immediately.</item>
                        <label>c.</label>
                        <item>Subject to advance consultation with appropriate members of Congress
                            additional Title I including about 400,000 MT wheat to become effective
                            when Congress passes PL–480
                            legislation.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Every possible effort made persuade Poles satisfy Canadian desires. Poles have
                    given general assurance US wheat will not displace Canadian sales but state
                    emphatically cannot make definite advance commitment to Canadians, especially in
                    view problem this would create re other countries. Dept considers US has fully carried out undertaking given to
                    Canadians. Canadian Embassy (Ritchie) informed by Kalijarvi today.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d368-f3"/> Informing
                        NATO tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d368-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d368-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 442.4841/5–2857. Official Use Only.
                    Drafted by Howard M. Gabbert and
                        John M. Leddy; cleared with ITR, BNA, E, and W; approved and
                    signed for Dulles by Leddy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d368-f2" n="2" xml:id="d368-f2-content">
                <p>An agreement with Poland was reached on June 7. For text, see Department of State
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, June 24, 1957, pp. 1005–1008.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d368-f3" n="3" xml:id="d368-f3-content">
                <p>No record of a conversation between Ritchie and Kalijarvi has been found in Department of State files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
